// Regression test: newline-separated top-level statements must not fuse.
//
// Bug: the self-hosted pratt.hv parser relied on `advance()` silently eating
// newlines, then the implicit-call sugar absorbed the next line's expression as
// a call argument. "print(\"a\")\nprint(\"b\")" became the single nested call
// print("a")(print("b")), so the teardown of __main__ tried to call the null
// result -> "Attempted to call non-callable value of type null".
// Semicolons worked; newlines did not.
//
// Expected: each newline-separated statement runs independently, ordering is
// preserved, and teardown returns cleanly (exit 0).

acc = []

acc.push(1)
acc.push(2)
acc.push(3)

assert(#acc == 3, "newline-separated statements did not all run")
assert(acc[0] == 1 && acc[1] == 2 && acc[2] == 3, "statement order not preserved")

x = 5
y = x + 2
z = y * 3
assert(x == 5 && y == 7 && z == 21, "newline-separated assignments failed")

print("newline stmt boundary ok")
